WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:03.163
- When I came to the TL,

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:05.730
you know, I'm an artist

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:08.970
and one of the projects I do is under,

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:10.000
it's under a pseudonym

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.770
and the first person that I
met that asked me my name,

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:15.603
I blurted it out.

00:00:15.603 --> 00:00:16.436
I'm like now or never

00:00:16.436 --> 00:00:17.363
so I said, Rogan.

00:00:20.239 --> 00:00:22.707
Using a different name,

00:00:22.707 --> 00:00:25.380
it creates this different
version of yourself.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:26.280
And you're still you,

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:28.493
but I like that.

00:00:29.861 --> 00:00:30.694
So it's like a different,

00:00:30.694 --> 00:00:33.163
and so I have like a
slightly different identity.

00:00:33.163 --> 00:00:34.465
- [Mark] Rogan it is.

00:00:34.465 --> 00:00:35.298
(laughs)

00:00:35.298 --> 00:00:36.160
- [Rogan] It can go either way.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:37.280
I guess we'll just play it by ear.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:39.330
- [Mark] Okay. So Rogan
where'd you grow up?

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:40.980
Where are you from originally?

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:42.260
- I'm from California.

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:44.140
I was born on Oahu

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:48.300
and my family moved to
Daly City when I was five

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.359
and we moved to

00:00:50.359 --> 00:00:51.750
Fresno

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:55.760
at the end of sixth grade when I was 11.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:58.370
And from Fresno,

00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:01.280
I lived in Fresno until I was 25

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:03.010
and then that's when I
started moving around.

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:07.560
I went to Los Angeles and from Los Angeles

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:11.070
I moved to Colorado after meeting my ex

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:13.670
at a tattoo convention that
we were both working at.

00:01:15.048 --> 00:01:16.710
And

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:19.970
then we got an RV and traveled

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:23.130
around the country for three
and a half years in an RV

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:25.360
and we came to San
Francisco the first time

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:26.300
and I just,

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:28.170
I fell in love with the city.

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:29.743
It's amazing here.

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:34.100
And I made it a point to come back.

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:36.300
We had this Epic trip
that we needed to take

00:01:37.385 --> 00:01:38.898
to rescue our friend,

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:39.731
we thought we were gonna rescue our friend

00:01:39.731 --> 00:01:42.330
from rehab in Florida. (laughs)

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:43.670
And it was a year,

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:45.100
took a year to come back to the city

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:46.720
and I've been here since then.

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:49.918
That was quite a while ago now.

00:01:49.918 --> 00:01:51.525
- [Mark] So how was your childhood?

00:01:51.525 --> 00:01:52.358
- Mh?

00:01:52.358 --> 00:01:53.480
- [Mark] How was your childhood?

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:54.517
- My childhood?

00:01:55.728 --> 00:01:57.630
It was interesting.

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:00.360
I mean, everyone has, you know.

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:03.433
It was rough in some ways,

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:08.300
both of my parents were drinkers

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:09.140
and

00:02:10.302 --> 00:02:12.380
my mother worked in the evening

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:14.860
and my dad

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:16.740
worked during the day

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:20.460
and so there was a lot
of time that I spent

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:21.610
just kind of on my own.

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:25.450
I really spent most of my
time as a kid on my own.

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:26.400
I had a best friend

00:02:28.318 --> 00:02:30.330
and their family lived right
across the street from us.

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:32.633
But other than that,
I was kind of a loner.

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:35.853
And my dad was,

00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:37.850
I said he was an alcoholic

00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:39.950
and he was also physically abusive.

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:42.740
But looking back on it now,

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:47.740
I mean, I've long since forgiven
him before he passed away.

00:02:48.470 --> 00:02:51.433
He was really the only
person that truly got me.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:54.390
But I guess,

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:56.390
you realize your parents are just people

00:02:58.169 --> 00:02:59.270
and I don't know how else really

00:02:59.270 --> 00:03:00.670
he would have dealt with me.

00:03:01.577 --> 00:03:04.123
(laughs) It's not right but,

00:03:05.669 --> 00:03:08.350
I was a really precocious
child to say the least

00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:11.400
and very persuasive and

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:12.502
wild.

00:03:12.502 --> 00:03:16.500
I'm five and seven years
older than my brothers

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:20.090
So I was an only child
for a period of time

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:24.490
so I was spoiled and
the center of attention,

00:03:24.490 --> 00:03:26.140
at least when I was really small.

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:31.433
When we lived in Daly City,

00:03:32.922 --> 00:03:34.100
as a kid, you don't,

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:35.760
a lot of kids I guess don't really know

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:37.270
what your financial situation is.

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:38.810
You don't have any concept of money

00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:43.310
and compared to different
levels of poverty that exist,

00:03:43.310 --> 00:03:47.920
I can't say that we were that stricken,

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:49.030
but when we were,

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:52.813
my grandparents supported us.

00:03:52.813 --> 00:03:55.440
And when my parents split up,

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:58.540
I was 14 and surprisingly,

00:03:58.540 --> 00:03:59.770
my brothers, not for them,

00:03:59.770 --> 00:04:01.610
but we all went and lived with my dad

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:05.160
who stayed in an apartment as
close as he could to my mom

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:07.590
as possible that he could not afford

00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:11.283
and we were just completely destitute.

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:17.950
A friend of mine had a
job at Jack in the Box

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:20.183
and that was how we ate,

00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:26.730
which was kind of awesome to

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:27.850
have those things

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:29.550
that you don't really
think about at the time,

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:31.570
but it was rough.

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:32.883
It was rough.

00:04:33.930 --> 00:04:35.320
- [Mark] When did drug use start for you?

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:40.320
- I started using hardcore
drugs when I was, well, 14.

00:04:40.930 --> 00:04:43.814
And once I started that,

00:04:43.814 --> 00:04:45.250
that was it.

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:50.053
I actually wanted to be a
junkie since I was a little kid.

00:04:50.053 --> 00:04:50.886
- [Mark] Really?

00:04:50.886 --> 00:04:51.719
- It sounds really weird

00:04:51.719 --> 00:04:55.410
but there was something
kind of like romantic

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:56.833
about it to me.

00:04:57.800 --> 00:04:58.840
Mysterious.

00:04:58.840 --> 00:04:59.690
And

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:02.650
I read a lot.

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:03.483
A lot.

00:05:03.483 --> 00:05:06.090
And once I read

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:08.620
Jack Kerouac, that was it.

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:10.100
It was over.

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:12.687
And I read

00:05:12.687 --> 00:05:15.870
"Big Sur" which definitely inspired me,

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:19.390
but one of his lesser known
books it's called "Tristessa"

00:05:19.390 --> 00:05:23.392
and it was about this Mexican junkie whore

00:05:23.392 --> 00:05:24.330
that he was in love with

00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:26.140
and she just sounds so

00:05:27.610 --> 00:05:30.660
wild and mysterious and untamed

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:33.290
and I wanted to,

00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:36.820
I wanted to be her and
I also wanted to be him

00:05:36.820 --> 00:05:37.850
in love with her.

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:38.913
Just the whole,

00:05:40.030 --> 00:05:41.360
the whole package.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:43.310
I was really enamored of it all

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:48.113
and I have to say that I
think I've experienced it now.

00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:52.500
I use heroin and I've

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:56.470
done heroin now for so long.

00:05:56.470 --> 00:05:59.820
I think that it's like a relationship.

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:00.780
Yeah, it's...

00:06:01.640 --> 00:06:03.363
I can't imagine the,

00:06:04.650 --> 00:06:07.840
I can't, I really can't imagine
parting ways permanently

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:10.420
but I take a break every once in a while

00:06:10.420 --> 00:06:11.253
and

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:13.613
I have,

00:06:13.613 --> 00:06:14.446
I loathe to admit it

00:06:14.446 --> 00:06:18.700
but I did stop for a year and a half once

00:06:18.700 --> 00:06:21.630
and I actually was happy. (laughs)

00:06:21.630 --> 00:06:24.300
But it is what it is.

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:26.300
I am not

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:27.760
unhappy.

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:31.110
I make my own misery,
but if I look at my life

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:32.190
I have to say that

00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:36.590
I've had exactly the life I wanted.

00:06:36.590 --> 00:06:39.190
As rough as sometimes have been,

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:41.110
it's really exciting

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:46.110
and for as much torture
as I put myself through,

00:06:46.190 --> 00:06:49.130
I realized, actually just last night,

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:51.473
how little stress I have in my life.

00:06:53.202 --> 00:06:56.580
I'm so grateful for that and so just...

00:06:56.580 --> 00:06:57.640
Money is awesome

00:06:57.640 --> 00:07:00.830
and I feel that this
is gonna be my my year,

00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:02.480
not to say that I haven't had it

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:04.440
and gone through plenty of it,

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:07.203
but I just have never really
given a shit about it.

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:10.870
Thank God. I always say,

00:07:10.870 --> 00:07:14.773
I can be rented but I can't be bought.

00:07:17.850 --> 00:07:20.690
We were watching some reality show

00:07:20.690 --> 00:07:23.650
and people, wealthy people
and all their problems

00:07:23.650 --> 00:07:24.750
and their stresses and I thought,

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:27.860
"God, thank God, I don't
care about any of that."

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:29.760
And we're so lucky.

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:31.140
It takes so little.

00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:35.100
Just hang out in our hotel
room or wherever it is.

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:38.683
At one point we rented a
walk-in closet for $20 a day

00:07:38.683 --> 00:07:42.610
in this really cool house in Russian Hill

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:45.143
and we were happy with that.

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:48.200
- [Mark] So you're living
in the Tenderloin now?

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:50.090
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:07:50.090 --> 00:07:51.300
- [Mark] You're living on the street?

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:52.560
- No, no.

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:55.410
I've been doing the hotel
circuit of the Tenderloin

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:59.600
for years now, since I came here,

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:01.360
and I'm over it.

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:02.240
Now, I'm over it.

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:04.100
I mean, it's exciting,

00:08:04.100 --> 00:08:06.051
but now it's not exciting anymore.

00:08:06.051 --> 00:08:08.980
Moving constantly, having to move around

00:08:08.980 --> 00:08:13.410
and I'm ready now to do something else.

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:15.480
I think I've found some
place in North Beach.

00:08:15.480 --> 00:08:17.529
A big warehouse.

00:08:17.529 --> 00:08:20.850
- [Mark] How have you
been supporting yourself?

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:21.683
- It varies.

00:08:22.884 --> 00:08:24.417
I have been,

00:08:24.417 --> 00:08:29.140
I have been a prostitute
in some fashion or other,

00:08:29.140 --> 00:08:30.680
basically my entire life

00:08:32.830 --> 00:08:35.800
and I'm not really into it anymore.

00:08:35.800 --> 00:08:36.780
Not to say that,

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:40.180
I mean, not that I shun the idea.

00:08:40.180 --> 00:08:44.353
Definitely, it's not the fun that it was,

00:08:44.353 --> 00:08:47.090
when I first came here,
it was like Shangri-La

00:08:47.090 --> 00:08:48.770
and a lot of women,

00:08:48.770 --> 00:08:52.000
all the women I know kind
of had the same goal.

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:56.160
It's empowering to find
yourself and be sexy

00:08:56.160 --> 00:09:00.160
and be somewhere where
everyone accepts that

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:01.990
and it's not something
that you're judged for

00:09:01.990 --> 00:09:03.480
and it's something that people assume

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:07.470
about you, and correctly, and it's cool,

00:09:07.470 --> 00:09:08.303
but

00:09:09.620 --> 00:09:10.800
I just,

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:12.150
I don't smoke crack anymore

00:09:14.504 --> 00:09:16.554
and that changes it, that changes things.

00:09:17.460 --> 00:09:18.333
So,

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:22.530
I dabble in other,

00:09:22.530 --> 00:09:25.440
if there's a hustle and
there's some money in it,

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:27.030
I'm into it.

00:09:27.030 --> 00:09:27.950
- [Mark] Did you find the line

00:09:27.950 --> 00:09:30.640
that you are willing
to cross to make money

00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:32.530
has changed over the years?

00:09:32.530 --> 00:09:36.660
- Yeah. Over the years
I've grown a conscience

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:38.920
or I should say that it's matured

00:09:41.515 --> 00:09:42.515
and I don't want to,

00:09:43.730 --> 00:09:44.810
I don't wanna be greedy

00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:47.523
and I don't wanna take
anything from anybody.

00:09:49.495 --> 00:09:51.180
I don't want anybody to,

00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:52.580
just having it,

00:09:52.580 --> 00:09:55.000
not to say that I'm an angel

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:58.380
and I'll probably be a
shoplifter until the day I die

00:09:58.380 --> 00:10:00.083
just because,

00:10:01.460 --> 00:10:04.140
but to wreck someone's life,

00:10:04.140 --> 00:10:06.050
to take their life savings

00:10:06.050 --> 00:10:08.250
and they have no recourse for that,

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:13.220
that's just not something
that I've ever been into.

00:10:13.220 --> 00:10:16.060
- [Mark] So your moral compass
is changing for the better?

00:10:16.060 --> 00:10:16.893
- Yeah.

00:10:16.893 --> 00:10:17.760
- [Mark] As you age.

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:18.860
- Yeah. I actually,

00:10:18.860 --> 00:10:21.370
I think about things now.

00:10:21.370 --> 00:10:23.370
I didn't use to definitely.

00:10:23.370 --> 00:10:24.203
But

00:10:25.690 --> 00:10:27.430
my moral compass has,

00:10:27.430 --> 00:10:28.743
it's got direction now.

00:10:29.904 --> 00:10:30.737
- [Mark] Do you have friends?

00:10:30.737 --> 00:10:32.020
- Yeah.

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:32.853
Yeah.

00:10:34.220 --> 00:10:38.170
I find it near to impossible to

00:10:39.370 --> 00:10:43.110
maintain communication
with my oldest friends.

00:10:43.110 --> 00:10:48.110
I have friends that are not
from this version of my life.

00:10:50.020 --> 00:10:52.633
Just like it is with my immediate family.

00:10:53.480 --> 00:10:55.120
What is there to say?

00:10:55.120 --> 00:10:58.323
Yeah, I'm doing this still.

00:10:59.450 --> 00:11:04.450
There's a certain amount of
shame that comes with that

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:08.520
and I've got to get over it
because it's really just me.

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:12.100
I'm really blessed in
that the people I've known

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:14.232
for a really long time

00:11:14.232 --> 00:11:17.070
have always accepted me

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:18.770
and picked up right where we left off

00:11:18.770 --> 00:11:21.760
and I think the only person
that's judging me is me

00:11:22.600 --> 00:11:26.060
but that's for the better,

00:11:26.060 --> 00:11:27.310
the best, as well.

00:11:27.310 --> 00:11:29.385
I mean, I need to look at myself.

00:11:29.385 --> 00:11:31.993
I've got to do something with myself.

00:11:35.180 --> 00:11:37.240
And it seems like everything's kind of,

00:11:37.240 --> 00:11:40.820
it's coming to a head and I feel good.

00:11:40.820 --> 00:11:43.680
I feel good about the direction I'm going

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:48.590
and I don't feel like
it's the last chance.

00:11:48.590 --> 00:11:51.079
I just feel like it's the time.

00:11:51.079 --> 00:11:51.912
It's the chance.

00:11:51.912 --> 00:11:52.745
- [Mark] So you're more
hopeful now than you've been

00:11:52.745 --> 00:11:53.600
in the past?

00:11:53.600 --> 00:11:55.160
- Yeah. Definitely.

00:11:55.160 --> 00:11:59.480
I feel finally that I have

00:11:59.480 --> 00:12:03.550
not just a direction,
but a vision, you know?

00:12:03.550 --> 00:12:05.500
I can kind of see it coming together

00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:06.553
and I can,

00:12:08.570 --> 00:12:11.680
I've found my self worth in there

00:12:11.680 --> 00:12:15.680
in that mix where before I doubted myself

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:17.690
and I guess my

00:12:17.690 --> 00:12:18.800
big deal is

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:22.980
one day I would finally find some success

00:12:22.980 --> 00:12:25.460
and everyone at the party would stop

00:12:25.460 --> 00:12:26.810
and you'd hear all the glasses clink

00:12:26.810 --> 00:12:29.990
and somebody would say,
"What is she doing here?

00:12:29.990 --> 00:12:33.150
She's an imposter, kick her out."

00:12:33.150 --> 00:12:35.735
So I don't feel that way anymore.

00:12:35.735 --> 00:12:37.200
I don't feel that way anymore.

00:12:40.425 --> 00:12:41.258
- [Mark] Did you find yourself

00:12:41.258 --> 00:12:42.220
getting depressed sometimes or?

00:12:42.220 --> 00:12:44.343
- Oh yeah. I'm really manic.

00:12:45.500 --> 00:12:47.940
I guess, I think that I'm what you-

00:12:47.940 --> 00:12:49.025
- [Mark] I mean, living on the street,

00:12:49.025 --> 00:12:50.280
it would be hard not to, right?

00:12:50.280 --> 00:12:51.427
- Well, like I said,

00:12:51.427 --> 00:12:52.766
I'm not living on the street.
- [Mark] (indistinct)

00:12:52.766 --> 00:12:54.176
- But then again,

00:12:54.176 --> 00:12:56.930
that could be less stressful than...

00:12:57.850 --> 00:12:58.860
- [Mark] But it sounds
like you're scrambling

